# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the linux-clang-asan preset (plan H1).
# Only leaks inside third-party code that we can't fix belong here, each with
# the reason. Our own leaks are bugs: fix them instead.

# OCCT keeps the table of presentation drivers in a static handle for the
# life of the process (TPrsStd_DriverTable::Get(), reached from XCAF).
leak:TPrsStd_DriverTable::Get
# OCCT's STEP reader leaks the text of each syntax error it records
# (StepFile_ReadData::AddError); only malformed STEP files reach it. OCCT is
# built without frame pointers, so LeakSanitizer's fast unwinder stops at
# the allocation itself and the suppression has to name it (a slow unwind
# makes the whole suite several times slower).
leak:StepFile_ReadData::AddError
leak:TCollection_AsciiString::allocate
